the most senior Catholic cleric ever to  be convicted of child sexual abuse  received a six year prison sentence in  Australia this morning  a jury found Cardinal George Pell guilty  of molesting two choir boys more than 20  years ago Seth Doane is outside the  Vatican with the downfall of one of the  church's most powerful officials Seth  good morning good morning Cardinal Pell  faced up to 50 years behind bars for  five counts of child sex abuse the  Vatican has not yet made any official  comment but they are running their own  investigation in Australia outside the  court  protesters denounced Pell and the  Catholic Church Pell appeared at the  sentencing in an open shirt without the  customary collar of a Catholic priest  Chief Judge Peter Kidd said Pell  conducted himself with staggering  arrogance but explained he directed the  jury not to make the Cardinal a  scapegoat for any perceived failings of  the Catholic Church the judge also noted  that he saw no evidence of remorse the  Cardinal maintains his innocence and his  legal team will appeal the conviction  the 77 year old would be eligible for  parole after three years and eight  months one of Pels victims said he did  not take any comfort in the sentence in  a us-based victim's adversity advocacy  group that supports those who have been  victims of clerical sex abuse said that  they were disappointed in the  comparatively light sentence  Gail Seth Doane reporting from Rome  thank you
 

